109.
Power of appropriate Government to make rules.
(1)
Subject to the other provisions of this Act, the appropriate Government may, by notification, make rules for carrying out
the provisions of this Act.
(2)
In particular, and without prejudice to the generality of the foregoing, such rules may provide for all or any of the
following matters, namely: -
(a)
the process of obtaining the prior consent under the first proviso to sub¬section (2) of section 2;
